# All handled API responses use HTTP 200. Check status SUCCESS/FAIL and errorCode in JSON.
# Business results are nested under data; X-Trace-Id matches the response traceId.
### HTTP Client / IntelliJ / VS Code REST Client
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
### Create book
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/books
Authorization: Basic reader change-me
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{"title":"Effective Java","author":"Joshua Bloch","price":45.00}

### Search, zero-based pages
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/books/search
Authorization: Basic reader change-me
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "java",
  "page": 0,
  "size": 10
}

### Read book
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/books/1
Authorization: Basic reader change-me
Accept: application/json

### Update
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/books/1
Authorization: Basic reader change-me
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{"title":"Effective Java","author":"Joshua Bloch","price":49.00}

### Place order
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Authorization: Basic reader change-me
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{"bookId":1,"quantity":2}

### Join orders and books
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/search
Authorization: Basic reader change-me
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "page": 0,
  "size": 10
}

### External API
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/external/google
Authorization: Basic reader change-me
Accept: application/json

### Delete (HTTP 200, status FAIL / errorCode CONFLICT when referenced by an order)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/books/1
Authorization: Basic reader change-me
Accept: application/json
